---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="What My Lab Tests collects (very little), what it doesn't, and the analytics it runs."
  path="/privacy/"
  crumbs={[{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Privacy', path: '/privacy/' }]}
>
  <div class="prose-tight max-w-3xl">
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-extrabold sm:text-3xl">Privacy</h1>
    <p>
      Short version: we have no accounts, no forms and no payments, so there's
      very little to collect.
    </p>
    <h2 class="mt-6 text-xl font-bold">What we collect</h2>
    <p>
      Standard analytics via Google Analytics 4 (loaded through Google Tag
      Manager): pages viewed, approximate location by city, device type, and
      which outbound lab links get clicked. We use it to see which comparisons
      help people. We don't collect names, phone numbers, health details or
      payment information — the site has nowhere to enter them.
    </p>
    <h2 class="mt-6 text-xl font-bold">What happens when you book</h2>
    <p>
      Clicking "Book" takes you to the lab's own website. From that point their
      privacy policy applies, not ours. Anything you share there — name,
      address, samples, reports — never passes through us.
    </p>
    <h2 class="mt-6 text-xl font-bold">Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      Only the ones Google Analytics sets for measurement. Block them and the
      site works exactly the same.
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-soft">
      Questions or deletion requests: hello@mylabtests.in.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
